{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5jYZ7vvq391Jc7jF7Hs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## <<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add a new error code `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This will be used when trying to confirm a shipment that is in CANCELLED status.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new endpoint:\n   ```\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): ResponseEntity<Shipment>\n   ```\n   This endpoint will:\n   - Fetch the shipment by ID (throw 404 if not found)\n   - Check if the shipment is CANCELLED (throw 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM if it is)\n   - If the shipment is CREATED or already CONFIRMED, update it to CONFIRMED status (idempotent)\n   - Save it and return it with 200 OK status\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add 5 test cases:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment transitions it to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without changes\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with correct error code\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n   - Test that a repeated confirm (retry scenario) succeeds\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nI considered creating a separate service layer for business logic, but this would be unnecessary architectural complexity. The existing repository pattern with direct controller logic handles the simple state transition perfectly, and adding a service would violate the \"do not modify files outside the shipment feature except tests\" constraint.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED):**\n   - Read: Fetch shipment from repository by ID\n   - Write: Update status to CONFIRMED, save to repository\n   - Return: 200 OK with updated Shipment JSON\n\n2. **Idempotent path (CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED):**\n   - Read: Fetch shipment from repository by ID  \n   - Check: Already CONFIRMED\n   - Write: Update status to CONFIRMED (no actual change), save to repository\n   - Return: 200 OK with Shipment JSON (unchanged)\n\n3. **Error: CANCELLED shipment:**\n   - Read: Fetch shipment from repository by ID\n   - Check: Status is CANCELLED\n   - Throw: ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\n   - Return: 409 Conflict with error envelope\n\n4. **Error: Not found:**\n   - Read: Attempt to fetch shipment from repository by ID\n   - Throw: ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n   - Return: 404 Not Found with error envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `confirm a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED` — Covers requirement that CREATED→CONFIRMED transitions work\n2. `confirm an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds` — Covers idempotency requirement\n3. `confirm a CANCELLED shipment returns 409` — Covers rejection of terminal state\n4. `confirm a non-existent shipment returns 404` — Covers not-found case\n5. `retry confirm by calling twice in sequence` — Covers the operations retry scenario explicitly mentioned\n\n---\n\n## <<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":739,"cache_read_input_tokens":16458,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":739},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"264cc6aa-7ca6-4b39-beb2-880709f61663","uuid":"86cd8e78-a96e-460f-b3a9-2246f9f92a27","timestamp":"2026-09-15T18:55:53.759Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5jYYdQkbjCQ4EADJu7u"}
